      "writtenOn": "2026-07-03T14:37:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As we discussed offline, in the case of SFDP:\n- one thread could have a session in its deletion list and instead of really deleting the associated vnet flows (but actually disabling them in the hardware). It would mark them \u0027retired\u0027 for a grace period (e.g. time based or main loop based)\n- packets in RX queues already marked by the hardware would lookup for the associated vnet flows, see that they are \u0027retired\u0027 and would follow the slow software path (recreate a session etc).\n- the thread would eventually reclaim the slots once the grace period ended",
      "parentUuid": "ede67449_28aff91c",
      "revId": "5394ce538c666a80cac8d5eb43cba608d3b64bf1",
